message.content:
Below is a practical, step‑by‑step guide you can follow (or adapt) to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for your e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole pipeline – from choosing a stack to deploying – and sprinkle in code snippets, best‑practice tips, and useful resources so you can hit the ground running.

---

## 1️⃣ Pick Your Tech Stack

| Goal | Recommended Framework | Why |
|------|-----------------------|-----|
| **Fast, component‑driven UI** | **React** (Create‑React‑App / Vite) | Huge ecosystem, great tooling, mature community |
| **Opinionated, batteries‑included** | **Vue 3** (Vite + Pinia) | Simpler learning curve, excellent docs |
| **Enterprise‑grade, full‑stack** | **Angular** | Strong typing, built‑in CLI, RxJS |
| **Static‑site generator** | **Next.js** (React) | Server‑side rendering, image optimisation, API routes |
| **Mobile‑first SPA** | **Nuxt.js** (Vue) | SSR + static generation, auto‑routing |

> **Tip:** If you already have a backend in Node.js, Next.js gives you a single‑repo solution with API routes. If you’re using Django or Rails, consider a separate SPA repo and consume a REST/GraphQL API.

---

## 2️⃣ Project Skeleton & Tooling

```bash
# Example with Vite + React
npm create vite@latest ecommerce-frontend --template react
cd ecommerce-frontend
npm install
```

### Core Dependencies

| Purpose | Package | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| State mgmt | **Redux Toolkit** (React) / **Pinia** (Vue) | Simplifies store logic |
| Routing | **React Router v6** / **Vue Router** | Declarative routing |
| Styling | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first) | Rapid prototyping, responsive utilities |
| HTTP client | **Axios** | Interceptors for auth & error handling |
| Form handling | **react-hook-form** / **VeeValidate** | Lightweight validation |
| Testing | **Jest** + **React Testing Library** / **Vue Test Utils** | Unit + integration tests |
| Linting | **ESLint** + **Prettier** | Code consistency |
| CI/CD | GitHub Actions / GitLab CI | Automated lint, test, build |

> **Optional**: Add **Storybook** for isolated component development.

---

## 3️⃣ Design & Wireframing

1. **Sketch the core pages**  
   - Home / Landing  
   - Product Listing (category, search, filters)  
   - Product Detail  
   - Cart & Checkout flow  
   - User Account (login, profile, orders)  
   - Admin Dashboard (optional)

2. **Use Figma / Adobe XD**  
   - Create reusable components (buttons, cards, modals).  
   - Export design tokens (colors, spacing, typography).

3. **Accessibility first**  
   - WCAG 2.1 AA compliance.  
   - Semantic HTML, ARIA labels, focus management.

---

## 4️⃣ Build the Component Hierarchy

```text
src/
├─ components/
│  ├─ ui/          # Buttons, Inputs, Modals
│  ├─ layout/      # Header, Footer, Sidebar
│  ├─ product/     # Card, Carousel, Rating
│  └─ cart/        # ItemList, Summary
├─ pages/
│  ├─ Home.jsx
│  ├─ Category.jsx
│  ├─ Product.jsx
│  ├─ Cart.jsx
│  └─ Checkout.jsx
├─ hooks/
│  └─ useAuth.js
├─ store/
│  └─ cartSlice.js
└─ services/
   └─ api.js
```

### Example: ProductCard (React)

```tsx
import { Link } from 'react-router-dom';
import { useCart } from '@/hooks/useCart';

export const ProductCard = ({ product }) => {
  const { addToCart } = useCart();

  return (
    <div className="border rounded p-4 flex flex-col">
      <Link to={`/product/${product.id}`}>
        <img src={product.imageUrl} alt={product.name} className="h-48 w-full object-cover mb-2" />
        <h3 className="font-semibold">{product.name}</h3>
      </Link>
      <p className="text-gray-600">${product.price.toFixed(2)}</p>
      <button
        onClick={() => addToCart(product)}
        className="mt-auto bg-blue-600 text-white py-2 px-4 rounded hover:bg-blue-700"
      >
        Add to Cart
      </button>
    </div>
  );
};
```

---

## 5️⃣ State Management

### Redux Toolkit (React)

```ts
// cartSlice.ts
import { createSlice, PayloadAction } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';

interface CartItem {
  id: number;
  quantity: number;
}

const initialState: CartItem[] = [];

export const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'cart',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    addItem(state, action: PayloadAction<number>) {
      const existing = state.find((i) => i.id === action.payload);
      if (existing) existing.quantity += 1;
      else state.push({ id: action.payload, quantity: 1 });
    },
    removeItem(state, action: PayloadAction<number>) {
      return state.filter((i) => i.id !== action.payload);
    },
    clearCart() {
      return [];
    },
  },
});

export const { addItem, removeItem, clearCart } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

### Pinia (Vue)

```ts
// cartStore.ts
import { defineStore } from 'pinia';

export const useCartStore = defineStore('cart', {
  state: () => ({
    items: [] as { id: number; quantity: number }[],
  }),
  actions: {
    add(id: number) {
      const item = this.items.find((i) => i.id === id);
      if (item) item.quantity += 1;
      else this.items.push({ id, quantity: 1 });
    },
    remove(id: number) {
      this.items = this.items.filter((i) => i.id !== id);
    },
    clear() {
      this.items = [];
    },
  },
});
```

---

## 6️⃣ API Integration

```ts
// services/api.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.REACT_APP_API_URL || '/api',
});

api.interceptors.request.use((config) => {
  const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
  if (token) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  return config;
});

export default api;
```

#### Example: Fetch Products

```tsx
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import api from '@/services/api';

const useProducts = () => {
  const [products, setProducts] = useState([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    api.get('/products').then((res) => {
      setProducts(res.data);
      setLoading(false);
    });
  }, []);

  return { products, loading };
};

export default useProducts;
```

---

## 7️⃣ Routing & Navigation

```tsx
// App.jsx
import { BrowserRouter as Router, Routes, Route } from 'react-router-dom';
import Home from '@/pages/Home';
import ProductDetail from '@/pages/Product';
import Cart from '@/pages/Cart';
import Checkout from '@/pages/Checkout';

function App() {
  return (
    <Router>
      <Header />
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/" element={<Home />} />
        <Route path="/product/:id" element={<ProductDetail />} />
        <Route path="/cart" element={<Cart />} />
        <Route path="/checkout" element={<Checkout />} />
      </Routes>
      <Footer />
    </Router>
  );
}
```

---

## 8️⃣ Authentication Flow

1. **Login Page** – POST `/auth/login` → store JWT in `localStorage` or HttpOnly cookie.  
2. **Protected Routes** – Wrap with `<RequireAuth>` component that checks token validity.  
3. **Refresh Token** – Use silent refresh or background fetch to keep session alive.  

```tsx
// RequireAuth.jsx
import { Navigate, useLocation } from 'react-router-dom';

export const RequireAuth = ({ children }) => {
  const location = useLocation();
  const token = localStorage.getItem('token');

  if (!token) return <Navigate to="/login" state={{ from: location }} replace />;

  return children;
};
```

---

## 9️⃣ Performance Optimisation

| Technique | How |
|-----------|-----|
| **Code splitting** | `React.lazy()` + `Suspense` |
| **Image optimisation** | Next.js Image component or `srcset` |
| **Lazy load lists** | IntersectionObserver or `react-window` |
| **Prefetch critical assets** | `<link rel="prefetch">` |
| **Bundle size audit** | Webpack Bundle Analyzer / Vite Inspect |

---

## 🔟 Testing Strategy

| Layer | Tool | Focus |
|-------|------|-------|
| Unit | Jest + React Testing Library | Component logic |
| Integration | Cypress | End‑to‑end flows (add to cart, checkout) |
| Visual | Storybook + Chromatic | UI regression |
| Accessibility | axe-core | WCAG compliance |

Example unit test:

```tsx
test('adds item to cart', () => {
  const { getByText } = render(<ProductCard product={mockProduct} />);
  fireEvent.click(getByText(/Add to Cart/i));
  expect(cartSlice.actions.addItem).toHaveBeenCalledWith(mockProduct.id);
});
```

---

## 🏗️ Deployment Pipeline

| Platform | Steps |
|----------|-------|
| **Netlify** | Connect repo → Build command (`npm run build`) → Publish directory (`dist`) |
| **Vercel** | Same as Netlify, but auto‑detects Next.js and optimises SSR |
| **Docker** | `docker build . -t ecommerce-frontend` → Push to registry → Deploy to Kubernetes or ECS |
| **CI** | GitHub Actions: lint → test → build → deploy |

Sample GitHub Action:

```yaml
name: CI/CD

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  build-deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3
        with:
          node-version: '20'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run lint
      - run: npm run test
      - run: npm run build
      - uses: peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v3
        with:
          github_token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
          publish_dir: ./dist
```

